<speak>We can make the support practical and limited to what you actually use. There is no need to turn it into a tour of every feature. A short session on locating correspondence and finding the ordinary contact information would be enough to start with. If you prefer, you can be at your own device during that session, but you would remain in control of it throughout. I would also suggest choosing a quiet time at home rather than fitting the demonstration between office interruptions. The point is to make the routine easier, not to add another task to an already crowded afternoon.</speak>